+# Scope and revision checklist
+
+- [x] FAA PD01–PD04 inspected first; failed/indexed routes not treated as missing-record proof.
+- [x] Previously unperformed UA175 fields and cited note chain selected; no repeat of completed UA93 accounting.
+- [x] Seven new displayed source entities preserved and read; image2/7 source dependence identified.
+- [x] Letter/email now held as qualified third-party representations; native and agency-release authentication still open.
+- [x] Three/two/one descriptions and75/31 versus18/24 fields preserved together; no preferred field/cause.
+- [x] Row6 digit uncertainty and untranscribed fields retained; no forced267, units or total conversation count.
+- [x] Interview1A/SF97 and actual UAL/custody/schema retrieval targets recorded, including contrary outcomes.
+- [x] Full relevant report page images/notes inspected; AI synopsis not accepted as a historical source.
+- [x] Reproducible supplied-input comparison with negative controls; no claim that code authenticates a call.
+- [x] Earlier sources/registers and original requirements remain unchanged; exact addition diffs supplied.
+- [x] Public payload excludes source images, signatures, personal/contact/card/network data, page HTML and temporary queries. Only reviewed research paraphrases, technical fields and source locators included.
+- [ ] Obtain original native/agency/control files and complete TEL01–TEL04. This bounded unit does not do so.
+- [ ] Close FAA, recorder/materials and steel criteria. No such completion claimed.
+- [ ] Public commit/push/ref and file verification — record actual outcome separately.
+
+The underlying scans carry redaction/security markings. This report does not infer declassification or publish the raw scans. Public notes distinguish the official Commission's already-public account from new mirrored source representations, without exposing masked identities or private case data. Review/verification here is not legal or historical certification.

