+# UA175: underlying letter and email recovered; call-count and duration-field conflicts preserved
+
+October 28, 2026. Existing AUD016-A1 / TC05-B105 / TC06-B110; TEL01–TEL04. This advances the original-record plan through a previously unread source chain. It does not authenticate the calls or complete the telephone investigation.
+
+## Actual acquisition
+
+The [public Flight175 folder](https://www.scribd.com/document/13499792/T7-B13-Flight-175-Calls-Fdr-Entire-Contents-Starfix-and-RINC) exposes seven page images. All seven entities were preserved unchanged and inspected. Reader6 is a July31,2002 United letter to the EDVA prosecutor, stamped **UASSI1-00032888**. Reader7 is a related email printout, **UASSI1-00032889**, also reproduced upside down in reader2. Reader3–5 is a three-page FBI interview representation; reader1 is a folder cover. These are third-party images of underlying records, not authenticated native emails, agency delivery receipts or a verified complete release. The letter's author signature is masked; the Commission attributes it to Jeff Plantz. No masked identity is reconstructed.
+
+The supported browser retrieved displayed images without login or the gated document-download action. The observed image URLs end in.jpg, but the captured image entities are WebP. That delivery-format observation is not an allegation about alteration. Temporary image-query data, page HTML, raw images, personal/contact/card/network fields and signatures are excluded from this public addition. [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json) identify the actual preserved entities and timing limitations.
+
+## U175-02 — three attempts, two reported connections, one substantiated conversation
+
+The letter reports GTE information for attempts at **08:52 /75seconds**, **08:56 /31seconds**, and **08:57 /267seconds**. It says GTE reported connections for the first two and no connection for the third. Its own inquiry could substantiate **one conversation**, while acknowledging the discrepancy remained unresolved. Possible confusion involving Flight93 is offered by that author as a hypothesis, not demonstrated by this review.
+
+The accompanying email supplies **08:52:01,08:56:19,08:57:28**, labels them Eastern, and likewise says the last did not connect. Its separate Flight93 list contains five labels. The two email representations are one source lineage, not two corroborations.
+
+The official [Commission staff report, physical90–91, note166](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/staff-report-sept2005.pdf#page=90) itself preserves **two completed calls versus one received communication**. Physical21 describes an approximately two-minute recollection. The report does not conceal this disagreement in its footnote. Attempts, network connection, receipt and conversation are not interchangeable units. Neither the letter nor this review selects a resolved count.
+
+## U175-03 — a concrete duration-field question
+
+The already held [UA175 summary, reader26](https://html.scribdassets.com/5bafzdomdce6sz3/images/26-6b763d149c.jpg) was previously checked only for its header. Its selected fields now read:
+
+| Source row / printed time | Duration Connect | Duration Operator | Scp Duration | Letter / note166 duration |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+|2 /08:52:01|18|0|75|75seconds|
+|5 /08:56:19|24|0|31|31seconds|
+
+The reported75/31 agree numerically with the **SCP** column, not the **Connect** column. That is a field-choice/source-mapping lead, not proof that the report used the wrong field. Native definitions, units, export rules and event/recipient joins remain missing. These could concern different stages; incorrect compilation/reading remains possible. No account is selected as controlling and no field is automatically conversation length.
+
+There are **11 visible rows**, not11 independently established people or conversations. All Connect entries have positive supplied readings or positive candidate readings; all11 Operator entries read0. The08:57:28 Connect entry remains **2?7**, with207/267 retained as candidates. It is not filled from the letter's267. Its SCP field was not accepted. A positive field alongside the letter/email's unconnected description warrants the definitions; it does not establish a conversation or fabricated records. [Safe transcriptions](ROW-FIELDS.json).
+
+## U175-05–07 — specific originals still needed
+
+The FBI interview's final paragraph says notes were placed in a **1A envelope** and sent to the file; its first page gives **San Francisco leadSF97**. These are concrete retrieval locators for the actual notes and version/custody chain. The interview includes approximate05:30 and06:00 passages and relayed speech. It does not provide calibrated call times. Its pronoun wording and the report's attendant description are preserved as wording differences, not authenticated caller identity, a clock conversion or advance knowledge.
+
+The letter's receiving-office no-recording/detailed-log account and the report's separately cited **July16,2004 UAL SAMC-to-WHQ telephone explanation** do not establish absence of GTE air-ground records. Generation, receipt, retained copies and disposal remain separate questions. Seek that actual UAL report, source/configuration support, written controller statement,1A notes and agency-held letter/email/native event returns. [Exact targets](OPEN-RECORDS.json). No new request was submitted.
+
+## Source dependence and a current description error
+
+The current reader explicitly labels its synopsis AI-enhanced. That synopsis assigns five calls toUA175 and no records toUA93, contrary to the displayed email's three/five distinction. This is a derivative-description error, not a historical FBI discrepancy. The synopsis was not used as evidence. Likewise, the Commission report cites the letter; the report and letter cannot be counted as independent measurements of the same calls.
+
+## Tests, limits and preserved scope
+
+[Verifier](verify_comparison.py) calculates the selected-field comparisons and row accounting, checks pinned inputs, and uses altered-field and mistaken-positive-means-connected controls. It tests supplied transcriptions and dependence rules, not glyph-reading accuracy, native field meanings or historical calls. No new OCR, clock fit, network decoding or physical test ran. [Results](RESULTS.json), [reading scope](READING-SCOPE.json), [claim locators](CLAIM-LOCATORS.json), [checklist](CHECKLIST.md) and [exact text additions](TEXT-CHANGES.diff).
+
+FAA PD01–PD04 still needs actual correction/receipt, signed action/no-action and case disposition/applicability records. Steel still needs native attribution/custody/preservation decisions. Recorder/materials work remains with its existing technical owner; its active NEADS source review was not duplicated or claimed complete here. All five original-record/testing requirements remain open. Earlier sources, contradictory values, reports and shared registers were not overwritten. Publication is a separate milestone; a verified public copy cannot complete those historical tests.

